
The mcp feature installs an MCP server over stdio, which is run rather than
linked. Its location is:

    <installed-root>/<triplet>/tools/libtmux/libtmux-mcp-server[.exe]

For manifest mode, <installed-root> defaults to the manifest's vcpkg_installed
directory. Classic mode defaults to <vcpkg-root>/installed; --x-install-root
overrides both.

The immutable 0.1.0-alpha.2 server takes one POSIX tmux socket path as its only
argument. Always pass it; omitting it falls back to inherited or default tmux:

    /tmp/tmux-1000/private

Later servers accept --socket-name or --socket-path and retain one positional
path on POSIX. Without a selector, they require a valid inherited TMUX route
and never fall back to the default server. Run --help before registering them.

Windows-enabled later releases expose only the four read-only psmux discovery
tools. See https://github.com/libtmux/libtmux-cxx#windows-through-psmux before
use.
